% ============================================================================
% Constraint C7 as an enforced error: VCDM-conformance violation  [EXERCISED 2026-07-28, check -k]
% ============================================================================
% Status (exercised 2026-07-28 with refinery-cli check -k, image digest
% sha256:88f1332e9aae356d91aef86aaaa3368be1b3931929fb3e10d87d65ab8a7fca8e):
%   - spec_ambiguity.problem (IncomeCred pinned to mdoc under a VcdmConformance
%     mandate) -> "Inconsistencies found in model:
%     spec_ambiguity::vcdm_conformance_violation(IncomeCred, income_format):
%     error." (no scope widening needed). Reproduced unchanged in the
%     2026-08-03 before/after battery. Verbatim verdict tables: vault A-008
%     spec-ambiguity-probe / A-004 constraint-sensitivity-variants.
%
% In-model instrument for the specification-ambiguity design-error class
% (vault C-048). An ambiguous/underspecified profile admits divergent
% conformant readings; C7 pins one reading, and a format that fails it is
% flagged rather than silently accepted.
%
% NOTE (model/prose gap this addresses): the VcdmConformance governance
% annotation is declared in vc_metamodel.refinery and asserted in every CSOK
% scenario, but NO predicate reads it -- C7 was, until now, unenforced. This
% predicate enforces it. Kept in its own file (do NOT import into csok.problem):
% under a C7 error, an open income format narrows to the VCDM-conformant three
% and clause 1 of governance_conflict would carry the UNSAT by a different
% route, muddying the error-vs-propagation division of labour.

import vc_metamodel.

% A credential required to be VCDM-conformant must use a VCDM-conformant format.
error vcdm_conformance_violation(Credential c, Formatted_Credential f) <->
    VcdmConformance::target(_, c),
    format(c, f),
    !conforms_vcdm(f).
